1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,450
NARRATOR: Respect is the relationship.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:12,679
ALEX: Okay, serious question. What actually makes a relationship healthy?

3
00:00:12,829 --> 00:00:14,606
SAM: Trust?

4
00:00:14,756 --> 00:00:17,687
MAYA: Not arguing all the time?

5
00:00:17,837 --> 00:00:20,539
JORDAN: Being able to be yourself?

6
00:00:20,689 --> 00:00:24,118
ALEX: Exactly. But what does that actually look like?

7
00:00:29,068 --> 00:00:36,914
NARRATOR: Relationships aren't just about dating. They include friendships, family relationships, classmates and people we care about.

8
00:00:39,064 --> 00:00:42,683
MAYA: Sorry, I don't really feel like coming today.

9
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:45,775
SAM: That's okay. Maybe another time.

10
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:49,698
NARRATOR: First: respect.

11
00:00:56,048 --> 00:01:02,273
NARRATOR: Respect means understanding that someone else's feelings, opinions and choices matter too.

12
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,916
SAM: Let me see your messages.

13
00:01:08,066 --> 00:01:11,303
JORDAN: I'd rather keep my messages private.

14
00:01:11,453 --> 00:01:15,088
SAM: But if we're friends, you should show me.

15
00:01:15,238 --> 00:01:19,260
JORDAN: Being friends doesn't mean I have to give up my privacy.

16
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:23,407
SAM: Fair enough.

17
00:01:25,957 --> 00:01:34,744
NARRATOR: Everyone has boundaries. That could mean needing personal space, keeping something private, or saying no to something you're uncomfortable with.

18
00:01:34,894 --> 00:01:40,306
NARRATOR: And remember: No means no. You don't have to feel guilty for setting a boundary.

19
00:01:42,356 --> 00:01:45,567
ALEX: Come on, just do it. Everyone else is.

20
00:01:45,717 --> 00:01:48,060
MAYA: I don't want to.

21
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,885
ALEX: Seriously? Don't be boring.

22
00:01:52,335 --> 00:01:55,031
NARRATOR: Pressure isn't respect.

23
00:01:55,181 --> 00:02:01,194
NARRATOR: You should never have to do something just to keep a friend, impress someone or prove that you care.

24
00:02:03,744 --> 00:02:07,600
JORDAN: When you didn't invite me yesterday, I felt left out.

25
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:11,831
SAM: I didn't realise you felt that way. I'm sorry.

26
00:02:11,981 --> 00:02:14,214
JORDAN: Thanks for listening.

27
00:02:15,364 --> 00:02:19,273
NARRATOR: Good communication doesn't mean you never disagree.

28
00:02:19,423 --> 00:02:29,306
NARRATOR: It means being honest about how you feel, listening to the other person and trying to solve problems without insulting, threatening or humiliating each other.

29
00:02:30,856 --> 00:02:34,506
NARRATOR: Sometimes, a relationship can become unhealthy.

30
00:02:34,656 --> 00:02:37,923
NARRATOR: Checking your phone or messages without asking

31
00:02:38,073 --> 00:02:40,711
NARRATOR: Telling you who you can and can't see

32
00:02:40,861 --> 00:02:43,485
NARRATOR: Put-downs and “jokes” that hurt

33
00:02:43,635 --> 00:02:46,433
NARRATOR: Making you feel guilty for saying no

34
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:49,780
NARRATOR: Jealousy, anger or threats when you disagree

35
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:52,376
NARRATOR: Pressure to “prove” that you care

36
00:02:55,126 --> 00:03:03,722
NARRATOR: Respect is the relationship. If something doesn't feel right, talk to someone you trust: a friend, family member, teacher or school counsellor.
